} </span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#A0A0A0;--shiki-light:#CF222E\">from</span><span style=\"--shiki-dark:#99FFE4;--shiki-light:#0A3069\"> \"#components/ui/button.tsx\"</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>For most apps, use the extension in the target pattern.</p>\n<h2 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h2>\n<p>If TypeScript cannot resolve a <code>#...</code> import, check that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the specifier starts with <code>#</code></li>\n<li>the <code>imports</code> entry is in the nearest <code>package.json</code></li>\n<li><code>moduleResolution</code> is set to <code>bundler</code></li>\n<li><code>resolvePackageJsonImports</code> is enabled</li>\n<li>the matching target exists after components are added</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If a component is installed but imports still point to <code>@/...</code>, check that\n<code>components.json</code> uses the same <code>#...</code> aliases as your package imports.</p>"
